From bb4cda84eb14d5a02a150958a8dbbfefd9f4e43d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 10:14:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: scmi: Handle unsupported limits notifier

As PERFORMANCE_NOTIFY_LIMITS is optionnal, treats unsupported SCMI limits
notifications as normal.

When notifier registration returns -EOPNOTSUPP continue and keep warnings
for real errors.

Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:GPT-5.3-Codex
Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Iea6832b80d0eaf1a0f00a60185247ab2892663ed
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/579161
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c
@@ -317,7 +317,7 @@ static int scmi_cpufreq_init(struct cpuf
 							SCMI_EVENT_PERFORMANCE_LIMITS_CHANGED,
 							&priv->domain_id,
 							&priv->limit_notify_nb);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret && ret != -EOPNOTSUPP)
 		dev_warn(&sdev->dev,
 			 "failed to register for limits change notifier for domain %d\n",
 			 priv->domain_id);
